      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.73,
      "end": 2.61,
      "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.96,
      "end": 16.55,
      "text": "A bit, but less than a dog. They need feeding and water every day, eggs collecting, and a coop clean once a week or so."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 20.33,
      "end": 25.74,
      "text": "A few chickens are happy in a medium garden, as long as the coop is secure and they get time to scratch around."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 28.7,
      "end": 33.713,
      "text": "That's the big one. The coop needs to be fox proof, with a solid lock and wire buried under the run."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 37.713,
      "end": 43.013,
      "text": "Hens are fairly quiet, just a bit of clucking. Roosters are the loud ones, and you don't need one to get eggs."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 46.563,
      "end": 51.453,
      "text": "A lot of people don't. Start with three hens, chickens are social and shouldn't live alone."
    }
